# Reverse proxy for a STAGE/LIVE host (ARC.5). Copy to ~/.config/mpmv/Caddyfile on the server.
# The site address comes from MPMV_SITE_ADDRESS in ~/.config/mpmv/caddy.env. Caddy sets
# X-Forwarded-Proto, which Django trusts through SECURE_PROXY_SSL_HEADER (settings/live.py).
#
# Client IP (CORE.5): Caddy overwrites X-Real-IP with the client address, so a value sent by the
# client never reaches the app. Django reads it only from the mpmv-net subnet
# (MPMV_TRUSTED_PROXY_HEADER and MPMV_TRUSTED_PROXIES in mpmv.env). If a CDN proxies the site,
# {client_ip} is the CDN's address unless Caddy trusts it: add a global options block such as
#   { servers { trusted_proxies static <CDN ranges>
#               client_ip_headers CF-Connecting-IP } }
# with the CDN's published ranges, and allow only those ranges to reach ports 80 and 443.
{$MPMV_SITE_ADDRESS} {
	encode zstd gzip
	reverse_proxy mpmv-app:8000 {
		header_up X-Real-IP {client_ip}
	}
}
